    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2GsmuGHYTLo4EvV2gVVbd8J)_\n\nBefore: once `pulse` was loaded, pressing `C-x o` failed with `apply: Wrong number of arguments: #<subr other-window>, 0`.\n\nAfter: `C-x o` switches windows normally. The line still pulses on window change, and through `pulsar`.\n\n`sp-faces` advised `other-window`, the scroll commands and `recenter-top-bottom` with `pulse-line` using `:after`. Because `pulse-line` is interactive (it's bound to `C-<return>`), nadvice used its empty `(interactive)` spec in place of the advised command's own spec, so `other-window` got no COUNT.\n\nHow: this drops the `advice-add` loop from `libraries/modules/ui/sp-faces.el` and from its literate doc `docs/tangles/sp-faces.org`. The doc's prose now says why the advice was removed. Those commands already pulse through `pulsar-pulse-functions` in `sp-windows`. The `C-<return>` binding and the `window-selection-change-functions` hook stay as they are.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_011YYQVRu1Rv32L6sD5UTozk)_",
